//! The typed operations' hand-written half (spec/typed-sidecar-operations).
//!
//! `operations.rs` is generated by meridian-design, one method per operation,
//! and each calls into this: read the plugin's params as the domain message,
//! stamp what only the sidecar knows, check the grant, send. This is the part
//! that does not vary by operation, which is why it is written once and the
//! part that does is generated.
//!
//! The deployment's configuration is the exception to a plugin acting as
//! itself: a command or query in the `config` domain -- linking an external
//! account, reading the deployment's accounts to link it to (W6.4) -- is
//! admitted only acting for an admin of the plugin, in a session opened by
//! Manage (the claims' level `admin`), a link only for an external account the
//! plugin itself reported (W2.8), and one naming a new account only for a
//! deployment admin. **Two named exceptions** (contract v13; W4.9's notes,
//! W4.12): filing a ticket and reading what the plugin filed are admitted
//! acting for a person at any level, and never as the plugin itself
//! ([`FOR_A_PERSON_AT_ANY_LEVEL`], the one place they are named).
//!
//! **A service account** (contract v21; W4.9, W4.15). Claims whose
//! `subject_kind` says the subject is a service account -- minted by the
//! dashboard only for a call it admitted through the act's door -- are
//! admitted exactly as a person's command under Open, and stamped with the
//! account's subject, its kind and its owner ([`stamp_of`]), so every store
//! records a service account, never a person. It administers nothing: every
//! `config` command and query is refused it, whatever it holds, but the two
//! named exceptions, filing a ticket and reading back what was filed.
//!
//! **A session's level decides what is sent for the person** (W4.9, W6.9).
//! Under `write` (Open), a command on an account in the write set; under
//! `admin` (Manage), the accounts read and the link, and nothing else, since
//! `admin` reaches no account's data; under `read` (View), nothing. An
//! assertion naming no level holds nothing.
//!
//! **By the role holding the act** (contract v15, decisions/033): the plugin
//! names no role on what it sends; the sidecar asks which of the plugin's
//! roles hold the topic among their generated grants, and admits the command
//! for `write` -- or the `config` act for `admin` -- on one of those roles in
//! the claims' per-role entries, the account among that role's write
//! accounts. Refused otherwise, naming each role that grants it and what the
//! person holds on it ("RecordHoldingsStatement is custody's, and Ada holds
//! read on custody"). Claims with no per-role entry are read as the one
//! role's on a plugin holding one, and refused on a plugin holding several.
//! Each act admitted for a person is logged with its level and the roles it
//! was admitted under.
//!
//! **A read is within the plugin's read scope** (W4.4, W4.11). Every query is
//! stamped with the scope, marked as applying, so the store answers an empty
//! one with nothing; and one naming an account outside it -- the field
//! matrix/scoped.tsv names, which the generated operation hands here -- is
//! refused before it leaves.
//!
//! A refusal is the call's gRPC status, chosen by what the caller should do
//! about it: `permission_denied` for a topic none of the plugin's roles
//! grants, an account outside the read scope, or the deployment's
//! configuration without a deployment admin,
//! `invalid_argument` for a number the wire does not carry,
//! `failed_precondition` for an external account nobody has linked,
//! `unavailable` when nothing serves the topic, `deadline_exceeded` when it
//! did not answer in time, `aborted` when it answered with a refusal --
//! `failed_precondition` when that refusal is an account not granted the
//! instance (REFUSAL_REASON_ACCOUNT_NOT_LINKABLE, W6.30), `already_exists`
//! for a venue account code an `ems`'s map holds already (contract v22).
//!
//! **From contract v22**: a command naming its record by ID alone -- an
//! order's release, check, approval, claim, placement, change, report or
//! acknowledgement, a locate's use ([`BY_ID_ALONE`]) -- is admitted on the
//! role's grant and stamped with the instance's write scope, narrowed to the
//! person's, marked as applying, for the book to hold the record's account
//! to (W4.9). A service account's claims carry the algorithm its call named,
//! checked against the version's declared algorithms on every command and
//! stamped (`algorithm_id`). The venue's catalogue is read as the plugin
//! itself ([`AS_ITSELF`]).
//!
//! Where one status covers refusals a plugin must tell apart, the refusal
//! carries a reason code beside it, from the typed-operations refusal
//! catalogue (spec/typed-sidecar-operations, section 7): a `Refusal`, encoded,
//! in the trailing metadata [`REFUSAL_METADATA`]. A plugin acts on the code;
//! the words are for a person reading a log, and may change.

use meridian_bus::{BusError, Stamp};
use meridian_domain::exact::Exact;
use meridian_domain::v1 as domain;
use meridian_domain::v1::{ExternalAccountsEvent, LinkExternalAccountRequest};
use meridian_pb::plugin::v1 as plugin;
use meridian_pb::v1::{
    AccessLevel, CallerAssertion, CallerClaims, Refusal, RefusalReason, SubjectKind,
};
use prost::Message;
use tonic::metadata::{MetadataMap, MetadataValue};
use tonic::{Code, Response, Status};

use crate::service::Sidecar;

/// The deployment's configuration: what a plugin sends here it sends only for
/// an admin of the plugin (W6.4).
const CONFIGURATION: &str = "platform.config.";
const LINK_EXTERNAL_ACCOUNT: &str = "platform.config.command.link-external-account";
/// A plugin's ticket, filed with the dashboard (PluginFilesTicket, W4.12).
pub(crate) const FILE_TICKET: &str = "platform.config.command.file-ticket";
/// What became of the tickets a plugin filed (ReadFiledTickets, W4.12).
pub(crate) const FILED_TICKETS: &str = "platform.config.query.filed-tickets";
/// The `config` topics sent for a person at any level -- `read`, `write` or
/// `admin` -- rather than only for an admin of the plugin: the two named
/// exceptions of W4.9's notes (contract v13, ruled 2026-10-03). Every other
/// `config` command and query stays an admin's, and none is ever sent for
/// the plugin as itself.
pub(crate) const FOR_A_PERSON_AT_ANY_LEVEL: [&str; 2] = [FILE_TICKET, FILED_TICKETS];
/// The venue's catalogue (ReadVenueCatalogue, W11.20, contract v22): a
/// `config` read an `ems` or an `oms` makes as itself, on start and after a
/// loss, like its own configuration -- a venue's offering, no account's data
/// and nothing of the deployment's configuration a person administers (the
/// main session's settlement, 2026-10-12). Sent for nobody, whatever
/// assertion the call carries.
pub(crate) const AS_ITSELF: [&str; 1] = ["platform.config.query.venue-catalogue"];
/// An `ems`'s venue account mapping (MapVenueAccount, W11.22, contract v22).
const MAP_VENUE_ACCOUNT: &str = "platform.config.command.map-venue-account";
/// The commands that name a record by its ID alone -- an order, a placement,
/// a change request or a locate -- and no account (contract v22; W4.9, W11;
/// the order-path plan's protos, point 8, ruled 2026-10-12): admitted on the
/// role's grant and stamped with the sending instance's write scope, narrowed
/// to the person's write access where it acts for one, which the book checks
/// the record's account against. The generated operations hand these no
/// account; a test holds this list to them.
pub(crate) const BY_ID_ALONE: [&str; 20] = [
    "meridian.v1.RequestOrderChangeRequest",
    "meridian.v1.RecordCheckRequest",
    "meridian.v1.DecideApprovalRequest",
    "meridian.v1.ReleaseOrderRequest",
    "meridian.v1.SetWorkingConditionRequest",
    "meridian.v1.CreatePlacementRequest",
    "meridian.v1.RequestPlacementChangeRequest",
    "meridian.v1.ReportPlacementRequest",
    "meridian.v1.ReportChargeRequest",
    "meridian.v1.AcknowledgeFlagRequest",
    "meridian.v1.RecordLocateUseRequest",
    // Contract v23 (W11.23, W11.24): executions named by their IDs alone.
    "meridian.v1.AcceptExecutionRequest",
    "meridian.v1.DontKnowExecutionRequest",
    // Contract v24 (W11.26 to W11.34): an order's instruction and its
    // booking named by the order, a booking by its ID, a give-up's answer by
    // its execution, a sleeve cross by the account its record names, and an
    // alert by its ID.
    "meridian.v1.SetAllocationInstructionRequest",
    "meridian.v1.BookOrderRequest",
    "meridian.v1.HandOffBookingRequest",
    "meridian.v1.CorrectBookingRequest",
    "meridian.v1.ReportGiveUpRequest",
    "meridian.v1.RecordSleeveCrossRequest",
    "meridian.v1.AcknowledgeAlertRequest",
];

/// The venue facts stamped from the venue account map (matrix/stamped.tsv's
/// `venue-account-map`, contract v22), each with the topic it is sent on.
const VENUE_FACTS: [(&str, &str); 3] = [
    (
        "meridian.v1.ReportExecutionRequest",
        "platform.book.command.report-execution",
    ),
    (
        "meridian.v1.RecordLocateRequest",
        "platform.book.command.record-locate",
    ),
    // Contract v23 (W11.25): a venue's value-date roll.
    (
        "meridian.v1.ReportValueDateRollRequest",
        "platform.book.command.report-value-date-roll",
    ),
];

/// A placement (CreatePlacement, W11.8, contract v22), whose connectivity
/// plugin the sidecar holds to the claims' connectivity_instance_ids.
const CREATE_PLACEMENT: &str = "meridian.v1.CreatePlacementRequest";
/// An order's change (W11.3, contract v22): a quantity change is never an
/// `ems`'s.
const REQUEST_ORDER_CHANGE: &str = "meridian.v1.RequestOrderChangeRequest";
/// The entry kind the book journals an unplaced fact under (W11.13).
const UNPLACED_KIND: &str = "unplaced-fact-recorded";
/// The orders read (W11.17, contract v22): a connectivity plugin's answers
/// only the orders behind placements naming its instance.
const LIST_ORDERS: &str = "meridian.v1.ListOrdersRequest";

/// The role whose venue facts take their account from the venue account map
/// (contract v22, W11.22).
const CONNECTIVITY: &str = "connectivity";
/// Where a plugin says which external accounts its connection reaches (W2.8).
const EXTERNAL_ACCOUNTS: &str = "meridian.v1.ExternalAccountsEvent";

/// Whether claims are a service account's (W4.9, contract v21): set only by
/// the dashboard, for a call it admitted through the act's door (W4.15).
pub(crate) fn is_service_account(claims: &CallerClaims) -> bool {
    claims.subject_kind == SubjectKind::ServiceAccount as i32
}

/// What the sidecar stamps on what it sends with `claims` (W4.9): the
/// subject; for a person, the delegation and its client beside them where
/// the assertion names one; for a service account, its kind and its owner
/// (contract v21), and never a delegation; and, where `with_prepared`, the
/// prepared change it was made from (contract v20). Default claims are the
/// plugin acting as itself: nobody stamped.
pub(crate) fn stamp_of(claims: &CallerClaims, with_prepared: bool) -> Stamp {
    if claims.subject.is_empty() {
        return Stamp::default();
    }
    let service_account = is_service_account(claims);
    let delegation = if service_account {
        String::new()
    } else {
        claims.delegation_id.clone()
    };
    Stamp {
        acting_for_subject: claims.subject.clone(),
        acting_through_client: if delegation.is_empty() {
            String::new()
        } else {
            claims.client_name.clone()
        },
        acting_through_delegation: delegation,
        prepared_call_id: if with_prepared {
            claims.prepared_call_id.clone()
        } else {
            String::new()
        },
        acting_for_kind: if service_account {
            SubjectKind::ServiceAccount as i32
        } else {
            SubjectKind::Unspecified as i32
        },
        owner_subject: if service_account {
            claims.owner_subject.clone()
        } else {
            String::new()
        },
        // The algorithm the call named (contract v22), on a service
        // account's alone; checked against the version's declared
        // algorithms before anything is sent ([`Sidecar::declared_algorithm`]).
        algorithm_id: if service_account {
            claims.algorithm_id.clone()
        } else {
            String::new()
        },
        // Decided per placement, where the command is sent (contract v22).
        connectivity_allowed: false,
        account_scope: None,
    }
}

// The tonic surface already returns `Result<_, Status>` everywhere; boxing the
// error here alone would buy nothing.
#[allow(clippy::result_large_err)]
impl Sidecar {
    pub(crate) fn instance_id(&self) -> &str {
        &self.identity.instance_id
    }

    /// A venue fact's account, stamped from the venue account map (contract
    /// v22; W11.22, matrix/stamped.tsv's `venue-account-map`): sent by a
    /// connectivity plugin, the account its `ems` mapped the fact's venue
    /// account code to on this instance, and empty -- never refused -- where
    /// nobody has, so the book keeps the fact unplaced (W11.13). Sent by a
    /// plugin holding another role that sends the row, and not
    /// `connectivity`, the account it named, as it named it. A plugin
    /// holding `connectivity` and another role that sends the row is read
    /// as its connectivity role wherever it names a code. A role that does
    /// not send the row gives no shortcut: a plugin holding `custody` and
    /// `connectivity` takes the map, never its custody links (Q42).
    pub(crate) async fn venue_mapped_account(
        &self,
        payload_type: &str,
        venue_account_code: &str,
        named: &str,
    ) -> Result<String, Status> {
        let sending: Vec<String> = match VENUE_FACTS.iter().find(|(fact, _)| *fact == payload_type)
        {
            Some((_, topic)) => self.roles_granting(topic),
            None => self.identity.roles.clone(),
        };
        let connectivity = sending.iter().any(|role| role == CONNECTIVITY);
        let other = sending.iter().any(|role| role != CONNECTIVITY);
        if !connectivity || (other && venue_account_code.is_empty()) {
            return Ok(named.to_string());
        }
        let configuration = self.configuration(self.clock.now_ns()).await?;
        let mapped = configuration
            .venue_account_map
            .iter()
            .flat_map(|map| map.mappings.iter())
            .find(|mapping| {
                mapping.connectivity_instance_id == self.instance_id()
                    && mapping.venue_account_code == venue_account_code
                    && !venue_account_code.is_empty()
            })
            .map(|mapping| mapping.account_id.clone())
            .unwrap_or_default();
        if mapped.is_empty() {
            tracing::info!(
                instance = self.instance_id(),
                payload_type,
                venue_account_code,
                "a venue's fact names a code no ems mapped on this plugin; sent with no account"
            );
        }
        Ok(mapped)
    }

    /// A plugin's params, read as the domain message they are on the wire.
    ///
    /// The params keep every field number of the domain message and drop only
    /// the stamped ones, so their encoding is the domain message's with those
    /// unset. Refused before registration, as every operation is.
    pub(crate) fn as_domain<P: Message, D: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        params: P,
    ) -> Result<D, Status> {
        self.admitted()?;
        D::decode(params.encode_to_vec().as_slice()).map_err(|failed| {
            Status::internal(format!(
                "the params did not read as the domain message: {failed}"
            ))
        })
    }

    /// A number the plugin sent, refused naming its field when it is outside
    /// what the wire carries: more than 18 decimal places, or 38 digits
    /// (decisions/023). The generated SDKs refuse these before sending; this
    /// is for a plugin that built its params by hand, and it runs before
    /// anything is stamped, so a malformed row never reaches the conductor or
    /// the street store. Nothing is rounded. An unset number is not checked
    /// here: whether one is required is the receiving component's to say.
    pub(crate) fn exact(
        &self,
        field: &str,
        value: Option<&meridian_pb::v1::Decimal>,
    ) -> Result<(), Status> {
        let Some(value) = value else {
            return Ok(());
        };
        Exact::from_wire(value).map(|_| ()).map_err(|out_of_range| {
            let refusal = format!("{field} {out_of_range}; it is refused rather than rounded");
            self.note_refusal(&refusal);
            Status::invalid_argument(refusal)
        })
    }

    /// An amount, whose number is checked as any other is, under the name of
    /// the field the plugin set.
    pub(crate) fn exact_money(
        &self,
        field: &str,
        value: Option<&domain::Money>,
    ) -> Result<(), Status> {
        self.exact(field, value.and_then(|money| money.amount.as_ref()))?;
        // From contract v18 a Money names its asset (decisions/023 as
        // amended): a fiat currency by its ISO 4217 code, or its cash
        // instrument; a token's code in currency_code, or neither, refused.
        // A plugin built before keeps the code it always sent.
        let built_at = self
            .registration()
            .map_or(0, |held| crate::contract::declared(&held.contract_version));
        if let Some(money) = value.filter(|_| built_at >= 18) {
            if let Err(refusal) = meridian_domain::money::asset_of(field, money) {
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                return Err(Status::invalid_argument(refusal));
            }
        }
        Ok(())
    }

    /// A business date the plugin named, a day that exists (contract v18,
    /// ruling 3 of 2026-10-09), or the refusal naming its field.
    pub(crate) fn dates_stand(&self, payload_type: &str, payload: &[u8]) -> Result<(), Status> {
        match crate::lake::dates_refused(payload_type, payload) {
            None => Ok(()),
            Some(refusal) => {
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                Err(Status::invalid_argument(refusal))
            }
        }
    }

    /// An enum value the plugin sent, refused naming its field when the
    /// contract does not define it: proto3 carries any number, so an asset
    /// class of 99 would otherwise reach the bus as though it were one
    /// (sdk-contract/asset-class-is-an-enum). The generated SDKs refuse these
    /// before sending; this is for a plugin that built its params by hand.
    /// Zero, the unspecified value, is defined: whether one is required is
    /// the receiving component's to say.
    pub(crate) fn known(&self, field: &str, value: i32, defined: bool) -> Result<(), Status> {
        if defined {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let refusal = format!("{field} is {value}, which the contract does not define");
        self.note_refusal(&refusal);
        Err(Status::invalid_argument(refusal))
    }

    /// The topic this instance sends on: its own identifier where the row
    /// names `{instance}`, so a plugin can speak only as itself.
    fn own_topic(&self, topic: &str) -> String {
        topic.replace("{instance}", self.instance_id())
    }

    fn granted(&self, topic: &str) -> Result<(), Status> {
        let registration = self.admitted()?;
        if registration.grants.may_publish(topic) {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let held = if registration.roles.is_empty() {
            "no role".to_string()
        } else {
            registration.roles.join(", ")
        };
        let refusal = format!("no grant for {topic}: this plugin holds {held}");
        self.note_refusal(&refusal);
        Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
    }

    /// An event: checked, published, and its identifier handed back.
    pub(crate) async fn publish_typed<D: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        message: D,
    ) -> Result<Response<plugin::Published>, Status> {
        let topic = self.own_topic(topic);
        self.granted(&topic)?;
        let message = self.kept_at_the_edge(payload_type, message)?;
        let payload = message.encode_to_vec();
        let message_id = self
            .bus
            .publish(&topic, payload_type, payload.clone(), None, None)
            .map_err(refused)?;
        if payload_type == EXTERNAL_ACCOUNTS {
            self.keep_reported(&payload);
        }
        Ok(Response::new(plugin::Published { message_id }))
    }

    /// The external accounts the plugin just said it reaches, the whole list,
    /// in place of the last: the ones a link may name (W2.8, W6.4).
    fn keep_reported(&self, payload: &[u8]) {
        if let Ok(event) = ExternalAccountsEvent::decode(payload) {
            *self.reported.lock().expect("reported lock poisoned") = event
                .accounts
                .into_iter()
                .map(|account| account.external_account_id)
                .collect();
        }
    }

    /// A query: checked, asked, and the domain reply handed back as its
    /// plugin-facing mirror, which it is on the wire. One of the deployment's
    /// configuration is asked only for a deployment admin, who is stamped on
    /// it (W6.4); any other carries no person (decisions/014). Every one
    /// carries the plugin's read scope, marked as applying, and one naming
    /// `account` outside it is refused here, first (W4.4, W4.11); `account`
    /// is `None` for a query matrix/scoped.tsv declares unscoped, and empty
    /// for one naming none, which the store answers for the whole scope.
    pub(crate) async fn call_typed<D: Message + Default, R: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        message: D,
        account: Option<String>,
        acting_for: Option<CallerAssertion>,
    ) -> Result<Response<R>, Status> {
        let topic = self.own_topic(topic);
        self.granted(&topic)?;
        let message = self.kept_at_the_edge(payload_type, message)?;
        self.dates_stand(payload_type, &message.encode_to_vec())?;
        let mut stamp = if AS_ITSELF.contains(&topic.as_str()) {
            Stamp::default()
        } else if topic.starts_with(CONFIGURATION) {
            let (claims, roles) = self.vouched_for_configuration(
                &topic,
                payload_type,
                acting_for.as_ref(),
                self.clock.now_ns(),
            )?;
            tracing::info!(
                instance = self.instance_id(),
                topic,
                by = claims.subject,
                at_level = level_named(claims.level),
                roles = roles.join(","),
                "read for a person"
            );
            stamp_of(&claims, false)
        } else {
            Stamp::default()
        };
        let scope = self
            .configuration(self.clock.now_ns())
            .await?
            .read_account_ids;
        if let Some(account) = account.filter(|account| !account.is_empty()) {
            if !scope.contains(&account) {
                let refusal = format!("{account} is not in this plugin's read scope");
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                return Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal));
            }
        }
        stamp.account_scope = Some(scope);
        let (_, payload) = self
            .bus
            .call_stamped(
                &topic,
                payload_type,
                message.encode_to_vec(),
                None,
                None,
                &stamp,
            )
            .await
            .map_err(refused)?;
        // A connectivity plugin reads the orders behind the placements naming
        // its instance, and the records of those alone (W11.17, as a
        // placement is heard at the instance it names, matrix/directed.tsv).
        // A plugin reading the row by another role reads it by its scope.
        if payload_type == LIST_ORDERS {
            let granting = self.roles_granting(&topic);
            if !granting.is_empty() && granting.iter().all(|role| role == CONNECTIVITY) {
                return mirrored(directed_orders(&payload, self.instance_id())?);
            }
        }
        mirrored(payload)
    }

    /// A command: checked against the grant, against the plugin's write scope
    /// for the account it names, and -- when it is sent for a person (W4.9) --
    /// against what the dashboard vouched that person may write; then asked,
    /// with the person stamped on the envelope. One to the deployment's
    /// configuration is checked instead against the person being a deployment
    /// admin, and a link against what the plugin reported (W6.4).
    pub(crate) async fn command_typed<D: Message + Default, R: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        message: D,
        account: Option<String>,
        acting_for: Option<CallerAssertion>,
    ) -> Result<Response<R>, Status> {
        let topic = self.own_topic(topic);
        self.granted(&topic)?;
        let message = self.kept_at_the_edge(payload_type, message)?;
        self.statement_stands(payload_type, &message.encode_to_vec())?;
        self.dates_stand(payload_type, &message.encode_to_vec())?;
        // A command naming no account names none: a statement from a plugin
        // built before v7 is admitted with no account (crate::older).
        let account = account.filter(|account| !account.is_empty());
        let now = self.clock.now_ns();
        if topic.starts_with(CONFIGURATION) {
            // An admin's act on the deployment's configuration, not a write
            // to an account: a link names an account nothing may write through
            // this plugin yet, since the link is what grants it (W4.11).
            let (claims, roles) =
                self.vouched_for_configuration(&topic, payload_type, acting_for.as_ref(), now)?;
            if topic == LINK_EXTERNAL_ACCOUNT {
                self.reported_by_this_plugin(&message.encode_to_vec(), now)
                    .await?;
                self.names_a_new_account_only_for_a_deployment_admin(
                    &message.encode_to_vec(),
                    &claims,
                )?;
            }
            if topic == MAP_VENUE_ACCOUNT {
                self.code_mapped_once(&message.encode_to_vec(), now).await?;
            }
            tracing::info!(
                instance = self.instance_id(),
                topic,
                by = claims.subject,
                at_level = level_named(claims.level),
                roles = roles.join(","),
                "sent for a person"
            );
            return self.ask_for(&topic, payload_type, message, &claims).await;
        }
        // Read where it decides: an account named, or a record named by its
        // ID alone, whose write scope travels with it (contract v22).
        let by_id_alone = account.is_none() && BY_ID_ALONE.contains(&payload_type);
        let write_scope = if account.is_some() || by_id_alone {
            self.configuration(now).await?.write_account_ids
        } else {
            Vec::new()
        };
        if let Some(account) = &account {
            if !write_scope.contains(account) {
                let refusal = format!(
                    "account {account} is outside this plugin's write scope: nobody may write \
                     it through this plugin"
                );
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                return Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal));
            }
        }
        let mut writes = None;
        let claims = match acting_for {
            None => CallerClaims::default(),
            Some(assertion) => {
                let (claims, roles) =
                    self.vouched_writer(&topic, payload_type, &assertion, account.as_deref(), now)?;
                writes = Some(person_writes(&claims, &roles));
                tracing::info!(
                    instance = self.instance_id(),
                    topic,
                    by = claims.subject,
                    service_account = is_service_account(&claims),
                    owner = claims.owner_subject,
                    at_level = "write",
                    roles = roles.join(","),
                    "sent for a person"
                );
                claims
            }
        };
        // A command naming its record by ID alone carries the write scope it
        // is held to (contract v22, W4.9): the instance's, narrowed to what
        // the person may write through it where it acts for one.
        let scope = by_id_alone.then(|| {
            write_scope
                .iter()
                .filter(|held| writes.as_ref().is_none_or(|writes| writes.contains(*held)))
                .cloned()
                .collect::<Vec<String>>()
        });
        // An ordered quantity is changed by `portfolio`, or by the `oms` as a
        // trader's alignment, and never by an `ems` (W11.3; step 5's Q20): a
        // plugin whose roles granting the change are neither is refused for
        // the order's state, before the book hears of it. Which of the two
        // others it is, the book reads from the order's own proposer.
        if payload_type == REQUEST_ORDER_CHANGE {
            let quantity =
                domain::RequestOrderChangeRequest::decode(message.encode_to_vec().as_slice())
                    .ok()
                    .and_then(|request| request.change)
                    .is_some_and(|change| change.kind == domain::OrderChangeKind::Quantity as i32);
            let granting = self.roles_granting(&topic);
            if quantity
                && !granting
                    .iter()
                    .any(|role| role == "portfolio" || role == "oms")
            {
                let refusal = format!(
                    "an ordered quantity is changed by portfolio, or by the oms as an \
                     alignment, and {} changes it as {}, which changes no quantity",
                    self.instance_id(),
                    granting.join(" and ")
                );
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                return Err(refused_for(
                    Code::Aborted,
                    refusal,
                    RefusalReason::OrderState,
                ));
            }
        }
        // A placement (contract v22, W11.8): whether the connectivity plugin
        // it names is one the claims say the caller may route through from
        // this ems -- linked, available, its users naming them. A
        // connectivity plugin creates no placement (ruled 2026-10-13). The
        // book refuses and records CONNECTIVITY_NOT_ALLOWED by it.
        let routed = (payload_type == CREATE_PLACEMENT).then(|| {
            let named = domain::CreatePlacementRequest::decode(message.encode_to_vec().as_slice())
                .map(|placement| placement.connectivity_instance_id)
                .unwrap_or_default();
            !named.is_empty() && claims.connectivity_instance_ids.contains(&named)
        });
        let unmapped = account.is_none();
        let reply: Response<R> = self
            .ask_routed(&topic, payload_type, message, &claims, scope, routed)
            .await?;
        self.count_unplaced(payload_type, unmapped, &reply.get_ref().encode_to_vec());
        Ok(reply)
    }

    /// A venue fact the book kept unplaced naming no account, counted for the
    /// plugin's admin view (contract v22, W11.13): a report's answer naming an
    /// unplaced fact with no account, or a locate sent with no account mapped
    /// and kept.
    fn count_unplaced(&self, payload_type: &str, unmapped: bool, reply: &[u8]) {
        let kept = match payload_type {
            "meridian.v1.ReportExecutionRequest"
            | "meridian.v1.ReportPlacementRequest"
            | "meridian.v1.ReportChargeRequest" => domain::FactReply::decode(reply)
                .ok()
                .and_then(|reply| reply.unplaced)
                .is_some_and(|fact| fact.account_id.is_empty()),
            "meridian.v1.RecordLocateRequest" => {
                unmapped
                    && domain::LocateReply::decode(reply)
                        .ok()
                        .and_then(|reply| reply.entry)
                        .is_some_and(|entry| entry.kind == UNPLACED_KIND)
            }
            _ => false,
        };
        if kept {
            self.unplaced
                .fetch_add(1, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed);
            self.changed.notify_one();
        }
    }

    /// Asked, with the person stamped on the envelope -- and the delegation
    /// they acted through, when the assertion named one (W4.9, contract v9),
    /// with its client's name beside it (contract v10) -- and the reply read
    /// as its plugin-facing mirror. Default claims are
    /// the plugin acting as itself: nobody stamped.
    async fn ask_for<D: Message, R: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        message: D,
        claims: &CallerClaims,
    ) -> Result<Response<R>, Status> {
        self.ask_routed(topic, payload_type, message, claims, None, None)
            .await
    }

    /// [`Self::ask_for`], with the write scope a command naming its record
    /// by ID alone is held to, marked as applying, and a placement's verdict
    /// on its connectivity plugin (contract v22).
    async fn ask_routed<D: Message, R: Message + Default>(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        message: D,
        claims: &CallerClaims,
        scope: Option<Vec<String>>,
        routed: Option<bool>,
    ) -> Result<Response<R>, Status> {
        // The prepared change the person made this from (W4.9, contract
        // v20), as the dashboard's assertion named it; never alone. A service
        // account's kind and owner beside its subject (contract v21), and the
        // algorithm its call named (contract v22).
        let mut stamp = stamp_of(claims, true);
        stamp.account_scope = scope;
        stamp.connectivity_allowed = routed.unwrap_or(false);
        let (_, payload) = self
            .bus
            .call_stamped(
                topic,
                payload_type,
                message.encode_to_vec(),
                None,
                None,
                &stamp,
            )
            .await
            .map_err(refused)?;
        mirrored(payload)
    }

    /// The claims a `config` topic is sent for, or the refusal: a person at
    /// any level for the two named exceptions, an admin of this plugin in a
    /// session opened by Manage for every other, and never the plugin as
    /// itself (W4.9's notes, W4.12).
    /// With the roles it was admitted under, for the log: none for the two
    /// named exceptions, admitted at any level on any role.
    pub(crate) fn vouched_for_configuration(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        acting_for: Option<&CallerAssertion>,
        now_ns: i64,
    ) -> Result<(CallerClaims, Vec<String>), Status> {
        if FOR_A_PERSON_AT_ANY_LEVEL.contains(&topic) {
            self.vouched_person(topic, acting_for, now_ns)
                .map(|claims| (claims, Vec::new()))
        } else {
            self.vouched_admin(topic, payload_type, acting_for, now_ns)
        }
    }

    /// Which of this plugin's roles hold `topic` among their generated
    /// grants (decisions/033, point 3): what a person's act is admitted by.
    fn roles_granting(&self, topic: &str) -> Vec<String> {
        self.contract.roles_granting(&self.identity.roles, topic)
    }

    /// Claims carrying no per-role entry -- from a dashboard older than this
    /// sidecar, during an upgrade's roll -- are read as the one role's on a
    /// plugin holding one, exactly the check before v15; on a plugin holding
    /// several, nothing is sent for the person until they carry roles. Fail
    /// closed (W4.9).
    fn without_roles(&self, claims: &CallerClaims) -> Result<(), Status> {
        if !claims.roles.is_empty() || self.identity.roles.len() <= 1 {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let refusal = format!(
            "{}'s claims carry no level per role, and {} holds {}: nothing is sent for a person \
             on a plugin holding several roles until the claims say their level on each",
            who(claims),
            self.instance_id(),
            self.identity.roles.join(" and ")
        );
        self.note_refusal(&refusal);
        Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
    }

    /// The claims of a person an assertion vouches for, at any level: what a
    /// ticket is filed for, and read back for (W4.12). A filing with no
    /// assertion is the plugin as itself, which never files.
    fn vouched_person(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        acting_for: Option<&CallerAssertion>,
        now_ns: i64,
    ) -> Result<CallerClaims, Status> {
        let refuse = |refusal: String| {
            self.note_refusal(&refusal);
            Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
        };
        let Some(assertion) = acting_for else {
            return refuse(if topic == FILE_TICKET {
                "a plugin files a ticket only for a person it acts for".to_string()
            } else {
                "a plugin reads what it filed only for a person it acts for".to_string()
            });
        };
        let verifier = self.verifier.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| {
            Status::unauthenticated(
                "this sidecar holds none of the dashboard's keys, so it can vouch for nobody",
            )
        })?;
        let claims = verifier
            .vouched(assertion, now_ns)
            .map_err(|refusal| Status::unauthenticated(refusal.said()))?;
        if !matches!(
            AccessLevel::try_from(claims.level),
            Ok(AccessLevel::Admin | AccessLevel::Write | AccessLevel::Read)
        ) {
            return refuse(format!(
                "{} holds no level on this plugin in this session, so nothing is sent for them",
                claims.subject
            ));
        }
        Ok(claims)
    }

    /// The claims of an admin of this plugin an assertion vouches for, in a
    /// session opened by Manage, or the refusal: the deployment's
    /// configuration is sent to only for one (W4.9, W6.4), and never by the
    /// plugin as itself.
    fn vouched_admin(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        acting_for: Option<&CallerAssertion>,
        now_ns: i64,
    ) -> Result<(CallerClaims, Vec<String>), Status> {
        let refuse = |refusal: String| {
            self.note_refusal(&refusal);
            Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
        };
        let Some(assertion) = acting_for else {
            return refuse(format!(
                "{topic} is the deployment's configuration: a plugin sends it only acting for \
                 an admin of the plugin, and this carries no assertion"
            ));
        };
        let verifier = self.verifier.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| {
            Status::unauthenticated(
                "this sidecar holds none of the dashboard's keys, so it can vouch for nobody",
            )
        })?;
        let claims = verifier
            .vouched(assertion, now_ns)
            .map_err(|refusal| Status::unauthenticated(refusal.said()))?;
        if is_service_account(&claims) {
            return refuse(never_administering(topic, &claims));
        }
        if claims.level != AccessLevel::Admin as i32 {
            return refuse(format!(
                "{topic} is the deployment's configuration: a plugin sends it only acting for \
                 an admin of the plugin in a session opened by Manage, and {}'s is {}",
                claims.subject,
                session_named(claims.level)
            ));
        }
        // By `admin` on a role whose grants include it (W4.9, decisions/033
        // point 2): the link is custody's, and an admin of the plugin's other
        // roles alone is refused it, naming custody.
        let granting = self.roles_granting(topic);
        self.without_roles(&claims)?;
        if claims.roles.is_empty() {
            return Ok((claims, granting));
        }
        let admitted: Vec<String> = granting
            .iter()
            .filter(|role| {
                claims
                    .roles
                    .iter()
                    .any(|held| &held.role == *role && held.level == AccessLevel::Admin as i32)
            })
            .cloned()
            .collect();
        if admitted.is_empty() {
            return refuse(format!(
                "{} is {}, and {} holds {}",
                act_named(topic, payload_type),
                owned_by(&granting),
                who(&claims),
                held_on(&claims, &granting)
            ));
        }
        Ok((claims, admitted))
    }

    /// A link naming a new account, rather than an existing one, is a
    /// deployment admin's: creating an account stays theirs (W6.3, W6.4).
    fn names_a_new_account_only_for_a_deployment_admin(
        &self,
        link: &[u8],
        claims: &CallerClaims,
    ) -> Result<(), Status> {
        let link = LinkExternalAccountRequest::decode(link)
            .map_err(|failed| Status::internal(format!("the link did not read: {failed}")))?;
        if link.new_account_name.is_empty() || claims.deployment_admin {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let refusal = format!(
            "{} is an admin of this plugin and not a deployment admin: a link names an \
             existing account, and only a deployment admin names a new one",
            claims.subject
        );
        self.note_refusal(&refusal);
        Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
    }

    /// A venue account code is mapped once per connectivity plugin (W11.22,
    /// contract v22): one this `ems`'s map holds at that plugin for another
    /// account is refused here, `already_exists` naming the code, before the
    /// conductor hears of it; the conductor refuses it too, for a map this
    /// sidecar has not been told yet.
    async fn code_mapped_once(&self, mapping: &[u8], now_ns: i64) -> Result<(), Status> {
        let asked = domain::MapVenueAccountRequest::decode(mapping)
            .map_err(|failed| Status::internal(format!("the mapping did not read: {failed}")))?;
        if asked.account_id.is_empty() {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let configuration = self.configuration(now_ns).await?;
        let held = configuration
            .venue_account_map
            .iter()
            .flat_map(|map| map.mappings.iter())
            .find(|held| {
                held.connectivity_instance_id == asked.connectivity_instance_id
                    && held.venue_account_code == asked.venue_account_code
            });
        match held {
            Some(held) if held.account_id != asked.account_id => {
                let refusal = format!(
                    "venue_account_code: {} is mapped on {} to {} already; remove that mapping \
                     first, and nothing was changed",
                    asked.venue_account_code, asked.connectivity_instance_id, held.account_id
                );
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                Err(refused_naming(
                    Code::AlreadyExists,
                    refusal,
                    RefusalReason::Unspecified,
                    vec!["venue_account_code".into()],
                ))
            }
            _ => Ok(()),
        }
    }

    /// A link names an external account this plugin said its connection
    /// reaches (W2.8), or -- to remove it -- one it already links. Any other
    /// is refused before the conductor hears of it.
    async fn reported_by_this_plugin(&self, link: &[u8], now_ns: i64) -> Result<(), Status> {
        let link = LinkExternalAccountRequest::decode(link)
            .map_err(|failed| Status::internal(format!("the link did not read: {failed}")))?;
        let external = link.external_account_id.as_str();
        if self
            .reported
            .lock()
            .expect("reported lock poisoned")
            .contains(external)
        {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let unlinking = link.account_id.is_empty() && link.new_account_name.is_empty();
        if unlinking
            && self
                .configuration(now_ns)
                .await?
                .links
                .iter()
                .any(|held| held.external_account_id == external)
        {
            return Ok(());
        }
        let refusal = format!(
            "external account {external} is not one this plugin reported: a plugin links only \
             the accounts its connection reaches (W2.8)"
        );
        self.note_refusal(&refusal);
        Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
    }

    /// The person an assertion vouches for, if they may write `account`
    /// through this plugin -- or, for a command naming none, anything at all
    /// through it -- with the roles it is admitted under. Their access is
    /// what the dashboard signed, under a minute ago; a person narrows what a
    /// plugin may do and never widens it.
    ///
    /// **By the role holding the act** (contract v15, decisions/033 point 3,
    /// W4.9): the person holds `write` on one of the plugin's roles whose
    /// generated grants include the command's topic, with the account among
    /// that role's write accounts; a row several roles hold is admitted for
    /// `write` on any of them. Otherwise refused, naming each role that
    /// grants it and what the person holds on it.
    fn vouched_writer(
        &self,
        topic: &str,
        payload_type: &str,
        assertion: &CallerAssertion,
        account: Option<&str>,
        now_ns: i64,
    ) -> Result<(CallerClaims, Vec<String>), Status> {
        let verifier = self.verifier.as_ref().ok_or_else(|| {
            Status::unauthenticated(
                "this sidecar holds none of the dashboard's keys, so it can vouch for nobody",
            )
        })?;
        let claims = verifier
            .vouched(assertion, now_ns)
            .map_err(|refusal| Status::unauthenticated(refusal.said()))?;
        let refuse = |refusal: String| {
            self.note_refusal(&refusal);
            Err(Status::permission_denied(refusal))
        };
        // The algorithm a service account's call named (contract v22, W4.9):
        // one this version declares, checked on every command the claims
        // carry it on, so none can name another; then stamped.
        if is_service_account(&claims) {
            if let Err(words) = self.declared_algorithm(&claims.algorithm_id) {
                let refusal = format!("algorithm_id: {words}");
                self.note_refusal(&refusal);
                return Err(refused_naming(
                    Code::InvalidArgument,
                    refusal,
                    RefusalReason::Unspecified,
                    vec!["algorithm_id".into()],
                ));
            }
        }
        // A command only in a session opened by Open: one under Manage
        // reaches no account's data, and one under View acts on nothing
        // (W6.9).
        if claims.level != AccessLevel::Write as i32 {
            return refuse(format!(
                "{} sent this in a {} session, and a command is sent for a person only in \
                 a session at write, opened by Open",
                claims.subject,
                session_named(claims.level)
            ));
        }
        let granting = self.roles_granting(topic);
        self.without_roles(&claims)?;
        if claims.roles.is_empty() {
            // One role, or none: the claims' write set is that role's, the
            // check before v15.
            let may_write = &claims.write_account_ids;
            return match account {
                Some(account) if !may_write.iter().any(|held| held == account) => {
                    Err(Status::permission_denied(format!(
                        "the person may not write account {account} through this plugin"
                    )))
                }
                None if may_write.is_empty() => Err(Status::permission_denied(
                    "the person may write nothing through this plugin",
                )),
                _ => Ok((claims, granting)),
            };
        }
        let mut admitted = Vec::new();
        let mut outside = Vec::new();
        for role in &granting {
            let Some(held) = claims
                .roles
                .iter()
                .find(|held| &held.role == role && held.level == AccessLevel::Write as i32)
            else {
                continue;
            };
            let writes: Vec<&str> = held
                .write_positions
                .iter()
                .filter_map(|at| claims.read_account_ids.get(*at as usize))
                .map(String::as_str)
                .collect();
            let reaches = match account {
                Some(account) => writes.contains(&account),
                None => !writes.is_empty(),
            };
            if reaches {
                admitted.push(role.clone());
            } else {
                outside.push(role.clone());
            }
        }
        if !admitted.is_empty() {
            return Ok((claims, admitted));
        }
        let act = act_named(topic, payload_type);
        if !outside.is_empty() {
            return refuse(match account {
                Some(account) => format!(
                    "{act} is {}, and {} holds write on {} without account {account}",
                    owned_by(&granting),
                    who(&claims),
                    outside.join(" and ")
                ),
                None => format!(
                    "{act} is {}, and {} may write no account on {}",
                    owned_by(&granting),
                    who(&claims),
                    outside.join(" and ")
                ),
            });
        }
        refuse(format!(
            "{act} is {}, and {} holds {}",
            owned_by(&granting),
            who(&claims),
            held_on(&claims, &granting)
        ))
    }
}

/// What a person may write through the plugin, as the claims vouch: on the
/// roles the command was admitted under, their write accounts there; from
/// claims carrying no per-role entry, their write set.
fn person_writes(claims: &CallerClaims, admitted: &[String]) -> Vec<String> {
    if claims.roles.is_empty() {
        return claims.write_account_ids.clone();
    }
    claims
        .roles
        .iter()
        .filter(|held| admitted.contains(&held.role) && held.level == AccessLevel::Write as i32)
        .flat_map(|held| held.write_positions.iter())
        .filter_map(|at| claims.read_account_ids.get(*at as usize))
        .cloned()
        .collect()
}

/// Who the claims name, for a refusal: their name where the dashboard gave
/// one, else their subject.
fn who(claims: &CallerClaims) -> &str {
    if claims.display_name.is_empty() {
        &claims.subject
    } else {
        &claims.display_name
    }
}

/// Why a service account's claims are refused a `config` topic (W4.9,
/// W6.32; contract v21): it administers nothing, whatever it holds.
pub(crate) fn never_administering(topic: &str, claims: &CallerClaims) -> String {
    format!(
        "{topic} is the deployment's configuration, and {} is a service account, which \
         administers nothing: whatever it holds, it is refused every config command and query \
         but filing a ticket and reading back what was filed",
        claims.subject
    )
}

/// The act a topic carries, as the matrix names its operation: the request's
/// type less its package and `Request` (`RecordHoldingsStatement`), or the
/// topic where no type is given.
fn act_named<'a>(topic: &'a str, payload_type: &'a str) -> &'a str {
    payload_type
        .rsplit('.')
        .next()
        .and_then(|name| name.strip_suffix("Request"))
        .filter(|name| !name.is_empty())
        .unwrap_or(topic)
}

/// "custody's", "custody's and operations'", or no role's.
fn owned_by(roles: &[String]) -> String {
    if roles.is_empty() {
        return "no role's this plugin holds".into();
    }
    roles
        .iter()
        .map(|role| {
            if role.ends_with('s') {
                format!("{role}'")
            } else {
                format!("{role}'s")
            }
        })
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join(" and ")
}

/// What the claims hold on each of `roles`: "read on custody", "nothing on
/// operations".
fn held_on(claims: &CallerClaims, roles: &[String]) -> String {
    if roles.is_empty() {
        return "no role that grants it".into();
    }
    roles
        .iter()
        .map(
            |role| match claims.roles.iter().find(|held| &held.role == role) {
                Some(held) => format!("{} on {role}", level_named(held.level)),
                None => format!("nothing on {role}"),
            },
        )
        .collect::<Vec<_>>()
        .join(" and ")
}

/// A session's level as a log names it.
pub(crate) fn level_named(level: i32) -> &'static str {
    match AccessLevel::try_from(level) {
        Ok(AccessLevel::Admin) => "admin",
        Ok(AccessLevel::Write) => "write",
        Ok(AccessLevel::Read) => "read",
        _ => "none",
    }
}

/// A session as the person chose it, for a refusal: by its button.
fn session_named(level: i32) -> &'static str {
    match AccessLevel::try_from(level) {
        Ok(AccessLevel::Admin) => "Manage (admin)",
        Ok(AccessLevel::Write) => "Open (write)",
        Ok(AccessLevel::Read) => "View (read)",
        _ => "level-less",
    }
}

/// A ListOrdersReply narrowed to one connectivity plugin's placements: the
/// orders behind them, their placements, executions and charges, and the
/// unplaced facts whose raw record it holds.
#[allow(clippy::result_large_err)]
fn directed_orders(payload: &[u8], instance: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>, Status> {
    let mut reply = domain::ListOrdersReply::decode(payload)
        .map_err(|failed| Status::internal(format!("the orders did not read: {failed}")))?;
    let mine = |placement: &domain::Placement| placement.connectivity_instance_id == instance;
    let placed: std::collections::BTreeSet<String> = reply
        .placements
        .iter()
        .filter(|placement| mine(placement))
        .map(|placement| placement.placement_id.clone())
        .chain(
            reply
                .orders
                .iter()
                .flat_map(|order| order.placements.iter())
                .filter(|placement| mine(placement))
                .map(|placement| placement.placement_id.clone()),
        )
        .collect();
    reply
        .orders
        .retain(|order| order.placements.iter().any(&mine));
    for order in reply.orders.iter_mut() {
        order.placements.retain(&mine);
        order
            .executions
            .retain(|execution| placed.contains(&execution.placement_id));
        order
            .charges
            .retain(|charge| placed.contains(&charge.placement_id));
    }
    reply.placements.retain(&mine);
    reply
        .executions
        .retain(|execution| placed.contains(&execution.placement_id));
    reply.unplaced_facts.retain(|fact| {
        fact.raw_record
            .as_ref()
            .is_some_and(|raw| raw.instance_id == instance)
    });
    Ok(reply.encode_to_vec())
}

/// A domain reply, read as the plugin-facing mirror it is on the wire.
#[allow(clippy::result_large_err)]
fn mirrored<R: Message + Default>(payload: Vec<u8>) -> Result<Response<R>, Status> {
    R::decode(payload.as_slice())
        .map(Response::new)
        .map_err(|failed| {
            Status::internal(format!("the reply did not read as its mirror: {failed}"))
        })
}

/// Where a refusal's reason code travels, beside its status.
pub const REFUSAL_METADATA: &str = "meridian-refusal-bin";

/// A refusal with its reason code from the catalogue beside the status.
pub(crate) fn refused_for(code: Code, words: String, reason: RefusalReason) -> Status {
    refused_naming(code, words, reason, Vec::new())
}

/// A refusal with its reason code and, for one naming what the command left
/// out, each field by its path (contract v9's REFUSAL_REASON_INCOMPLETE).
pub(crate) fn refused_naming(
    code: Code,
    words: String,
    reason: RefusalReason,
    fields: Vec<String>,
) -> Status {
    let mut metadata = MetadataMap::new();
    metadata.insert_bin(
        REFUSAL_METADATA,
        MetadataValue::from_bytes(
            &Refusal {
                reason: reason as i32,
                fields,
            }
            .encode_to_vec(),
        ),
    );
    Status::with_metadata(code, words, metadata)
}

pub(crate) fn refused(failed: BusError) -> Status {
    match failed {
        BusError::NoHandler(topic) => Status::unavailable(format!("nothing serves {topic}")),
        timeout @ BusError::Timeout { .. } => Status::deadline_exceeded(timeout.to_string()),
        // A component's refusal of its own (W9's book, contract v8), its
        // reason code carried beside the status and its words alone in it.
        // The fields it names as left out, where it names any, ride with it.
        // A component's refusal with a status and no code (contract v22): a
        // command it reads as malformed, naming each field, or a record whose
        // account is outside the write scope stamped on it (W4.9).
        BusError::HandlerFailed { detail, .. }
            if meridian_bus::read_refusal_status(&detail).is_some() =>
        {
            let (status, fields, words) =
                meridian_bus::read_refusal_status(&detail).expect("matched above");
            refused_naming(
                match status {
                    meridian_bus::RefusalStatus::InvalidArgument => Code::InvalidArgument,
                    meridian_bus::RefusalStatus::PermissionDenied => Code::PermissionDenied,
                },
                words.to_string(),
                RefusalReason::Unspecified,
                fields,
            )
        }
        BusError::HandlerFailed { detail, .. } => match meridian_bus::read_refusal(&detail)
            .and_then(|(reason, words)| Some((RefusalReason::try_from(reason).ok()?, words)))
        {
            // A store that could not check the command, nothing recorded:
            // to be tried again, so the status a caller retries (contract
            // v10). Every other refusal of a component's is `aborted`.
            Some((reason, words)) => refused_naming(
                match reason {
                    RefusalReason::ReferenceUnavailable => Code::Unavailable,
                    // An account not granted the instance, for a link or an
                    // `ems`'s mapping: the admin asks a deployment admin to
                    // grant it (W6.4, W6.30, W11.22).
                    RefusalReason::AccountNotLinkable => Code::FailedPrecondition,
                    _ => Code::Aborted,
                },
                words.to_string(),
                reason,
                meridian_bus::refusal_fields(&detail),
            ),
            None => Status::aborted(detail),
        },
        BusError::NotPublishable(topic) => {
            Status::invalid_argument(format!("`{topic}` is not a publishable topic"))
        }
        other => Status::internal(other.to_string()),
    }
}

